Every year on the first Sunday in May, blessings for members of commercial fishing fleets who have lost their lives at sea are held in Blaine and Bellingham, the Washington cities where almost all of the investor victims were from. One of Mark Colthurst's sisters always attends and makes sure to memorialize Mark, Irene, Kimberly, and John Colthurst, as well as Chris Heyman, Dean Moon, Jerome Cowan, and Michael Stewart. The investor murders remains the largest ever unsolved mass murder in the state of Alaska. There is still speculation as to who was responsible. Some are convinced John Peale was guilty. Others believe the drug smuggling theory. It's also been suggested that the culprit and their motives will remain forever unknown.
每年5月的第一个星期日，在布莱恩和贝灵厄姆（几乎所有投资者号受害者所在的华盛顿城市）都会为在海上遇难的商业渔船船员举行祈福仪式。马克·科尔瑟斯特的一位姐妹总是参加，并确保纪念马克、艾琳、金伯利和约翰·科尔瑟斯特，以及克里斯·海曼、迪恩·穆恩、杰罗姆·考恩和迈克尔·斯图尔特。投资者号谋杀案仍然是阿拉斯加州历史上最大的未破大规模谋杀案。关于谁该负责，仍有各种猜测。有些人确信约翰·皮尔有罪。另一些人相信毒品走私理论。也有人认为，罪魁祸首及其动机将永远不为人知。

